{
  "id": "SP060",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Ovarian cystectomy",
  "description": "An ovarian cystectomy is a minimally invasive surgery to remove a fluid-filled sac (a cyst) from your ovary, usually while keeping the ovary itself intact. Your doctor may recommend it when a cyst causes pain, grows large, does not go away on its own, or looks concerning on imaging. Your surgeon makes a few small incisions in your lower abdomen and uses a camera and specialized tools, typically under general anesthesia, to carefully remove the cyst. Most people go home the same day or after a short stay and recover within a couple of weeks. The goal is to relieve symptoms and protect your ovary and future fertility when possible.",
